<title>FRANCE: EP welcomes EU aid to combat drugs in third world.</title>
<headline>EP welcomes EU aid to combat drugs in third world.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Parliament on Thursday approved a new European Union programme designed to help developing countries combat drug abuse -- COM(95)296.</p>
<p>Fighting drugs would only be effective if its main root cause -- abject poverty -- was tackled first, Euro-MPs stressed in a report drafted by German Christian Democrat Peter Liese.</p>
<p>The report urged the EU to help provide people in developing countries with legal alternatives to the cultivation of lucrative drug crops.</p>
<p>It should only support projects where respect for human rights is agreed, parliament said.</p>
</text>
